{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CNN Dense Layer Integration.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CNN Dense Layer Integration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cnn dense layer integration cnn dense layer integration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CNN Dense Layer Integration.md","fileName":"CNN Dense Layer Integration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CNN Dense Layer Integration","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 02:14\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Convolutional Visual Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Convolutional Visual Architecture","Convolutional Neural Network","CNN Filter Bank","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CNN Dense Layer Integration.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CNN Dense Layer Integration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cnn dense layer integration cnn dense layer integration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CNN Dense Layer Integration.md","fileName":"CNN Dense Layer Integration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CNN Dense Layer Integration","heading":"CNN Dense Layer Integration","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A dense layer near the end of a [[Convolutional Neural Network]] can connect each of its neurons to all outputs from earlier filters. Unlike the shared weights within a convolutional filter, each dense neuron learns its own weights for combining those inputs.\n\nThis stage lets different neurons integrate the [[CNN Filter Bank|filter bank's]] local detections in different ways, such as relating simpler visual patterns to a whole-object decision. It is not another convolution: the dense connections collect information across the filter outputs rather than repeatedly applying one kernel to neighboring patches.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Convolutional Visual Architecture","